@page "/"
@using PullbackStrategyLab.Web.Shell
@model IndexModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "The lab";
}
@*
    The front door. It is the shell itself rather than a redirect to the watchlist, because the
    watchlist is empty until 4.1 and a front door that lands on an empty screen tells a reader
    nothing about what they are looking at.
*@
<h1>PullbackStrategyLab</h1>
<p class="lede">A paper-trading laboratory that tests two mirror-image price patterns on US
   equities every night, records every setup it flags whether or not it trades it, and improves
   the selection rules from that record. No real money, ever.</p>

<h2>The screens</h2>
<ul class="screens">
    @foreach (NavigationItem item in Navigation.Items)
    {
        <li>
            <a href="@item.Path">@item.Title</a>
            <span class="what">@item.What</span>
            <span class="when">checkpoint @item.ArrivesAt</span>
        </li>
    }
</ul>

<h2>The shared chart</h2>
<p class="lede">Every chart in the lab is one component, built here so no later checkpoint
   invents a second one. It has no bars until checkpoint 1.10 puts the store behind it, and it
   says so rather than drawing an empty box.</p>

@await Html.PartialAsync("_Candlestick", Model.Chart)
